-- title:
--   Admissible field of small constants, case q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose elements are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. the rational affine geometric places whose value at the generic $j$-invariant lies in `ssJSet`. Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from the base-changed full-level field to that level-$M'$ field (a valuation subring, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, a degree-preserving map of places, and compatibility with $A$), satisfying $hR_0$: for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image is an $R_0$-integer and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, let $\zeta$ be an index of a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and let $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$, indexed by $W$, be families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ subject to the Igusa conditions (the ring at the line at infinity is described by quotients of Laurent series over $A$; the family is transitive under $\Gamma_0(M')$ through `levelAutBar`, injective, and permuted by all level automorphisms) and the supersingular conditions (the constants cut out exactly $A$; $R_0$-residues and place evaluations control membership and congruences modulo the maximal ideal; invariance under level automorphisms; existence of a transversal element $t$), summarised here. Finally let $K_0$ be a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over it and $\pi\in K_0$, let $A_0$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with an injective local homomorphism $\iota : A_0\to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A\cap K_0$ and which is surjective onto the residue field of $A$, with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi_0$ and $\iota(\varpi_0)=\pi$, and let $F_0$ be the subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of series all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image of $j_q$ and carrying an $A_0$-algebra structure whose structure map is induced by $\iota$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $k_0$ and $K_0$ have the same underlying set, $\pi_0=\pi$, the ring $A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$, there is a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$ together with a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $k_0$, there is a unit $u$ of $A$ with $\pi_0^{q^2-1}=qu$, and there is a ring isomorphism $A_0\simeq A\cap k_0$ compatible with $\iota$.
--
--   This is the $q=2$ case of the step verifying that the descent field used for the Igusa-chart model is an admissible field of small constants: it repackages the given henselian base $A_0$, uniformiser $\pi$ and descent subfield $K_0$ as an intermediate field $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $A\cap k_0$ a henselian discrete valuation ring having the required uniformiser, residue field and roots of unity. It feeds the construction of the smooth Igusa and Drinfeld base models over the level field, and is cited by the statements producing the bottom-layer level field and the formal smoothness of the Igusa subalgebra at $q=2$.
